{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you, be fruitful and multiply.</b> He juxtaposed the command of procreation to the shedding of human blood, to teach you that whoever does not engage in procreation is as though he sheds blood. And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in Yevamot: whoever does not engage in procreation is as though he sheds blood and diminishes the Divine likeness. Rabbi Akiva says: as though he reduces the Divine likeness. Others say: he causes the Shekhinah to withdraw from Israel, as it is said (Genesis 17:7): ״להיות לך לאלהים ולזרעך אחריך״ — 'to be an Elohim to you and to your seed after you.' When your seed is after you — the Shekhinah dwells; if your seed is not after you — upon whom does it dwell? Upon the trees or upon the stones? One must understand what 'diminishes the Divine likeness' means, and also the language of Rabbi Akiva, who said 'as though he reduces the Divine likeness' and did not say 'diminishes.' And Scripture says (Isaiah 13:4): ״קול המון בהרים דמות עם רב, ה' וכלי זעמו לחבל כל הארץ״ — 'The voice of a multitude in the mountains, the likeness of a great people; YHWH and the weapons of His wrath to destroy all the earth.' And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: 'the likeness of a great people' — this is the Holy One, blessed be He. <br><b>And further,</b> in the Midrash on ״דמיתיך רעיתי״ — 'your likeness, my beloved' — there is no דמיתיך except likeness, teaching that in likenesses the Holy One, blessed be He, revealed Himself to Israel, like a person who pictures his fellow and says, 'this is So-and-so.' So Israel would gaze upon the Holy One, blessed be He, and picture Him and say, 'This is my El and I will glorify Him' — therefore it says, ״דמיתיך רעיתי.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:27.842622536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}